Feature: Phase 13 Statuses File
  `fts/ft.db` is gitignored, so a scenario's status is lost on a fresh clone.
  `fts/statuses.csv` is a git-tracked snapshot of each scenario's *current*
  status only, not a full history log. `ft init` creates it, `Store.InsertStatus`
  upserts into it, and `ft sync` (not `ft init`) reconstructs the database
  from `.ft` files plus this file whenever it finds `fts/ft.db` missing — the
  same code path that handles ordinary reconciliation, since
  `OpenProjectStore` already creates and migrates a fresh DB file
  transparently if one doesn't exist. Full status history remains DB-only.

  Background:
    Given the user has run `ft init`

  @ft:201
  Scenario: Init creates the statuses file
    Given fts/statuses.csv does not exist
    When  the user runs `ft init`
    Then  fts/statuses.csv is created
    And   the file contains the header row "id,status"

  @ft:202
  Scenario: Init leaves an existing statuses file alone
    Given fts/statuses.csv already exists with status entries
    When  the user runs `ft init`
    Then  fts/statuses.csv is unchanged

  @ft:203
  Scenario: Statuses file is not added to gitignore
    Given a .gitignore file exists
    When  the user runs `ft init`
    Then  fts/statuses.csv is not listed in .gitignore

  @ft:204
  Scenario: Setting a status upserts the scenario's row in the statuses file
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with Scenario "User logs in" as @ft:1
    When  the user runs `ft status 1 accepted`
    Then  fts/statuses.csv has a row with id 1, status "accepted"

  @ft:205
  Scenario: Sync's automatic modified status updates the statuses file
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with Scenario "User logs in" as @ft:1
    And   scenario 1 has status "accepted"
    When  the user changes the steps of scenario 1 in fts/login.ft
    And   the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  fts/statuses.csv has a row with id 1, status "modified"

  @ft:206
  Scenario: Sync's automatic removed status updates the statuses file
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with Scenario "User logs in" as @ft:1
    And   the user has set scenario 1 to "accepted"
    When  the user removes the scenario from fts/login.ft
    And   the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  fts/statuses.csv has a row with id 1, status "removed"

  @ft:207
  Scenario: Sync's automatic restored status updates the statuses file
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with Scenario "User logs in" as @ft:1
    And   scenario 1 has been removed
    When  the user re-adds the scenario with its original @ft:1 tag
    And   the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  fts/statuses.csv has a row with id 1, status "restored"

  @ft:208
  Scenario: New file with an unclaimed tag keeps the tagged id
    Given a fresh database with no files or scenarios recorded
    And   fts/login.ft exists on disk with Scenario "User logs in" already tagged @ft:42
    And   no scenarios record exists with id 42
    When  the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  the scenarios record for id 42 is created with name "User logs in"
    And   no new id is assigned to the scenario

  @ft:209
  Scenario: New file with an untagged scenario still gets a fresh id
    Given a fresh database with no files or scenarios recorded
    And   fts/login.ft exists on disk with an untagged Scenario "User logs in"
    When  the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  a new scenarios record is created
    And   the assigned id is written to the file as an @ft:<id> tag

  @ft:210
  Scenario: Sync recreates scenarios from tagged files after ft.db is deleted
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with Scenario "User logs in" as @ft:1
    And   fts/ft.db is deleted
    When  the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  a fresh fts/ft.db is created with a migrated schema
    And   the scenarios record for id 1 is recreated with name "User logs in"

  @ft:211
  Scenario: Sync restores current status from the statuses file after a rebuild
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with Scenario "User logs in" as @ft:1
    And   the user has set scenario 1 to "accepted"
    And   the user has set scenario 1 to "in-progress"
    And   fts/ft.db is deleted
    When  the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  scenario 1 has exactly one status record
    And   that status is "in-progress"
    And   fts/statuses.csv is not modified by the rebuild

  @ft:215
  Scenario: Sync backfills DB-only status into the statuses file even when the file already has other rows
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with scenarios "User logs in" and "User fails login"
    And   the user has set scenario 2 to "in-progress"
    And   scenario 1 has a current status of "accepted" recorded only in the database
    And   fts/statuses.csv already contains a row for scenario 2 but not scenario 1
    When  the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  fts/statuses.csv gains a row with id 1, status "accepted"
    And   fts/statuses.csv still has the row for scenario 2

  @ft:214
  Scenario: Sync does not replay the statuses file into an already-populated database
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with Scenario "User logs in" as @ft:1
    And   the user has set scenario 1 to "accepted"
    When  the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  no additional status records are inserted into the statuses table for scenario 1

  @ft:212
  Scenario: Rebuild skips status history with no matching scenario
    Given fts/statuses.csv has a "removed" row for id 99
    And   no .ft file contains an @ft:99 tag
    And   fts/ft.db is deleted
    When  the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  no scenarios record for id 99 is created
    And   no error is raised
    And   the "removed" row for id 99 still exists in fts/statuses.csv

  @ft:213
  Scenario: Rebuild rediscovers test links
    Given fts/login.ft has been synced with Scenario "User logs in" as @ft:1
    And   cmd/login_test.go contains "// @ft:1" above "func TestLogin" at line 5
    And   ft sync has been run to discover the link
    And   fts/ft.db is deleted
    When  the user runs `ft sync`
    Then  the test_links table contains a row for scenario_id 1
